<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<PLUGIN name="intel.gpu.firmware" author="Intel GPU Firmware contributors" version="2026.11.24i-alpha2" launch="Tools/IntelGpuFirmware" icon="/plugins/intel.gpu.firmware/intel-gpu-firmware.png" min="7.4.1" pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/centauri/unraid-intel-gpu-firmware/alpha/intel.gpu.firmware.plg" support="https://github.com/centauri/unraid-intel-gpu-firmware/issues">
  <CHANGES>2026.11.24i-alpha2 — Functional public alpha with confirmed GSC updates
Unlike alpha 1, this release can write compatible newer GSC firmware using Intel IGSC.
Installation and plugin updates never flash automatically. Every GPU update requires
fresh identity/image/maintenance checks and explicit exact-device confirmation.
No force, downgrade, arbitrary firmware upload or automatic retry. UPS remains optional.
2026.11.24h-alpha1 — Public alpha, physical writes disabled
Separate recoverable preflight from uncertain writes; consume failed plans.
Restore after failed rehearsals and resume partial restoration safely.
Re-arm guards after simulated reboot; reserve changed device mappings conservatively.
Show exact hardware evidence, add interruption tests and a read-only alpha update channel.
2026.11.24g — Targeted GPU maintenance
Review GPU users, stop only affected workloads, and guard Docker/libvirt starts.
Preserve restart policies and original running states; rehearse without flashing.
Keep guards on uncertain outcomes and require post-reboot verification before restore.
2026.11.24a — Optional UPS advice
A UPS is recommended, not required. Missing or unhealthy monitoring is advisory.
Keep firmware identity, compatibility, device-use and explicit confirmation checks.
Use a version suffix that sorts after the previous release in Unraid's string comparison.
2026.11.24.9 — Firmware history and Intel release checks
Persist observed versions, compatible GSC images and update outcomes per PCI identity.
Import the existing update journal without another flash; avoid duplicate USB writes.
Check Intel's official package page on request; retain old results on connection/parser failure.
Discovered packages never replace the trusted catalog or enable a firmware update.
Correct the timeout message so it cannot deny a preceding firmware write.
2026.11.24.8 — Final target revalidation
Recheck PCI identity, driver and MEI mapping immediately before the native write.
2026.11.24.7 — Hardened update workflow and separate candidate
Reject Intel diagnostics even when the CLI returns zero; check its version transcript.
Invalidate old plans and recheck maintenance after persisting intent.
Test the shared background worker, locking, duplicate requests and failed writes.
The standard build remains read-only. A separate candidate allows confirmed GSC writes.
2026.11.24.6 — Tools tile and GPU icon
Open the tool from its own System Information tile instead of embedding it in Tools.
Add a GPU circuit-board icon to the tile, plugin listing and page header.
2026.11.24.5 — Read-only live validation
Scope GPU facts styling against Unraid's global definition-list styles.
Record native PHP, device, download, dry-run and HTTP rejection evidence.
2026.11.24.4 — Preserve CSRF validation after Unraid's prepend
Decode the original bounded form after Unraid removes the validated token from POST.
Use one version source for plugin metadata and static asset cache keys.
2026.11.24.3 — Native Unraid integration fixes
Use an outer form CSRF token for Unraid's PHP security prepend.
Version static assets so reinstallations do not retain stale browser code.
2026.11.24.2 — Read-only test build
Native firmware writes are blocked in the API, engine and process executor.
Added non-writing dry tests against the real detected card.
2026.11.24.1 — Initial preview
Generic Intel display-controller detection across board vendors.
Pinned firmware catalog, hardware compatibility checks and explicit GSC update plans.
No automatic firmware updates. OPROM and board data remain read-only.
</CHANGES>
  <FILE Run="/bin/bash">
    <INLINE>set -e
test "$(uname -m)" = x86_64 || { echo "This build requires x86_64 Unraid."; exit 1; }
mkdir -p /var/lib/intel-gpu-firmware
exec 9&gt;/var/lib/intel-gpu-firmware/work.lock
flock -n 9 || { echo "Firmware operation in progress."; exit 1; }
</INLINE>
  </FILE>
  <FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/intel.gpu.firmware/payload-482cc6785c09d0d86bb1b4190e9d381a71cf705de3d24adccae7a127a33fd266.tar.gz" Type="base64">
    <INLINE></INLINE>
  </FILE>
  <FILE Run="/bin/bash">
    <INLINE>set -e
printf '%s  %s\n' '482cc6785c09d0d86bb1b4190e9d381a71cf705de3d24adccae7a127a33fd266' '/boot/config/plugins/intel.gpu.firmware/payload-482cc6785c09d0d86bb1b4190e9d381a71cf705de3d24adccae7a127a33fd266.tar.gz' | sha256sum -c -
#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail
umask 077
cache=/boot/config/plugins/intel.gpu.firmware
runtime=/var/lib/intel-gpu-firmware
backend=/usr/local/libexec/intel-gpu-firmware
payload="$cache/payload-482cc6785c09d0d86bb1b4190e9d381a71cf705de3d24adccae7a127a33fd266.tar.gz"
mkdir -p "$cache" "$runtime"
# Installation, reinstallation and removal must not replace a running worker.
exec 9&gt;"$runtime/work.lock"
flock -n 9 || { echo "A firmware operation is running. Try again after it finishes."; exit 1; }
php -r 'if(PHP_VERSION_ID&lt;80100)exit(1); foreach(["pcntl_fork","posix_kill","simplexml_load_string","fsync"] as $f)if(!function_exists($f))exit(1);' ||
  { echo "PHP 8.1+, pcntl, POSIX, SimpleXML and fsync are required."; exit 1; }
if [ -f "$cache/state/maintenance.json" ]; then
  php -r '$s=json_decode(file_get_contents($argv[1]),true); if(!is_array($s))exit(1); if($s &amp;&amp; ($s["state"]??"")!=="complete" &amp;&amp; ($s["boot_id"]??"")===trim(file_get_contents("/proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id"))) {fwrite(STDERR,"Restore GPU maintenance before reinstalling.\n");exit(1);}' "$cache/state/maintenance.json"
fi
if [ -f "$cache/state/flash.json" ]; then
  php -r '$v=json_decode(file_get_contents($argv[1]),true); if (!is_array($v)) exit(1); $same=($v["plan"]["boot_id"]??"")===trim(file_get_contents("/proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id")); if ($same &amp;&amp; in_array($v["state"]??"",["preflight","flashing","verifying","needs_attention"],true)) {fwrite(STDERR,"An interrupted firmware update needs attention; installation stopped.\n");exit(1);}' "$cache/state/flash.json"
fi
fetch() {
  local file=$1 hash=$2 url=$3
  if [ ! -f "$cache/$file" ] || ! printf '%s  %s\n' "$hash" "$cache/$file" | sha256sum --status -c -; then
    curl --fail --silent --show-error --location --proto '=https' --proto-redir '=https' --connect-timeout 20 --max-time 180 "$url" -o "$cache/$file.partial"
    printf '%s  %s\n' "$hash" "$cache/$file.partial" | sha256sum -c -
    mv "$cache/$file.partial" "$cache/$file"
  fi
}
fetch igsc.deb bb7b8d2fad24d017f17a057684c459176ec7ea483cabc622e8ac68f27c560727 'https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/i/igsc/igsc_1.3.2+~metee6.2.6-5_amd64.deb'
fetch libigsc.deb 14cf0b016add49a4843a6e52364605614b2ad759f8a9e2c1e268ac92092ddee0 'https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/i/igsc/libigsc1_1.3.2+~metee6.2.6-5_amd64.deb'
fetch 7zip.tar.xz 2b539cf067b2ad48e1baa5093dbaa8818b73542d1222a0ffde9dc5f2922ea62e 'https://github.com/ip7z/7zip/releases/download/26.06/7z2606-linux-x64.tar.xz'
tmp=$(mktemp -d /tmp/intel-gpu-firmware-install.XXXXXX)
trap 'rm -rf -- "$tmp"' EXIT
mkdir -p "$tmp/igsc" "$tmp/libigsc" "$tmp/root" "$tmp/7zip"
bsdtar -xf "$cache/igsc.deb" -C "$tmp/igsc"
bsdtar -xf "$cache/libigsc.deb" -C "$tmp/libigsc"
tar -xJf "$tmp/igsc/data.tar.xz" -C "$tmp/root"
tar -xJf "$tmp/libigsc/data.tar.xz" -C "$tmp/root"
tar -xJf "$cache/7zip.tar.xz" -C "$tmp/7zip"
# Validate the dependency bundle before changing the installed plugin.
LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$tmp/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu" "$tmp/root/usr/bin/igsc" --version
"$tmp/7zip/7zz" i &gt;/dev/null
tar -xzf "$payload" -C "$tmp"
mkdir -p "$backend/vendor/bin" "$backend/vendor/lib" "$backend/vendor/licenses"
cp "$tmp/root/usr/bin/igsc" "$backend/vendor/bin/"
cp -a "$tmp/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/"libigsc.so* "$backend/vendor/lib/"
cp "$tmp/7zip/7zz" "$backend/vendor/bin/"
cp "$tmp/7zip/License.txt" "$backend/vendor/licenses/7zip.txt"
mkdir -p "$backend/vendor/licenses/debian"
cp -a "$tmp/root/usr/share/doc/." "$backend/vendor/licenses/debian/"
cp "$tmp/src/"*.php "$backend/"
cp "$tmp/catalog/catalog.json" "$backend/catalog.json"
cp "$tmp/LICENSE" "$backend/LICENSE"
mkdir -p "$backend/docs"
cp "$tmp/docs/"* "$tmp/README.md" "$backend/docs/"
chmod 0755 "$backend/vendor/bin/"*
mkdir -p /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/intel.gpu.firmware
cp "$tmp/web/"* /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/intel.gpu.firmware/
chmod -R go-w "$backend" /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/intel.gpu.firmware
# Static assets must be readable by the web server; private state stays root-only.
chmod 0755 /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/intel.gpu.firmware
chmod 0644 /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/intel.gpu.firmware/*
php "$backend/maintenance-boot.php"
echo "Intel GPU Firmware installed. Open Tools &gt; Intel GPU Firmware. No GPU was flashed."
</INLINE>
  </FILE>
  <FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
    <INLINE>#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail
mkdir -p /var/lib/intel-gpu-firmware
exec 9&gt;/var/lib/intel-gpu-firmware/work.lock
flock -n 9 || { echo "A firmware operation is running. Removal stopped."; exit 1; }
maintenance=/boot/config/plugins/intel.gpu.firmware/state/maintenance.json
if [ -f "$maintenance" ]; then
  php -r '$s=json_decode(file_get_contents($argv[1]),true); if(!is_array($s)||($s&amp;&amp;($s["state"]??"")!=="complete"))exit(1);' "$maintenance" ||
    { echo "Restore GPU maintenance before removing the plugin."; exit 1; }
fi
state=/boot/config/plugins/intel.gpu.firmware/state/flash.json
if [ -f "$state" ]; then
  php -r '$v=json_decode(file_get_contents($argv[1]),true); if(!is_array($v)||!in_array($v["state"]??"",["complete","not_started"],true))exit(1);' "$state" ||
    { echo "An interrupted firmware operation needs attention. Removal stopped."; exit 1; }
fi
rm -rf -- /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/intel.gpu.firmware /usr/local/libexec/intel-gpu-firmware
echo "Plugin removed. Firmware was not changed. Cached downloads and update history remain on the boot device."
</INLINE>
  </FILE>
</PLUGIN>